IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `types`
IMPORT `chapter-3-punishments`
IMPORT `chapter-4-exceptions`
IMPORT `chapter-4a-private-defence`

§ `Chapters 6A and 6B -- Piracy and genocide`

-- Penal Code 1871 ss 130B, 130C, 130D, 130E.
-- Source: registers/source-bundle/PC1871.txt.
--
-- Two short Chapters. Chapter 6A: piracy by the law of nations (s 130B), which the
-- Code does not define but adopts, and the four piratical acts on a Singapore ship
-- (s 130C), which it does. Chapter 6B: genocide (s 130D), the five acts with the
-- intent to destroy a group, and its punishment (s 130E), which splits on whether the
-- offence consists of killing.
--
-- s 130B(2)'s aggravated punishment -- death where the pirate murders, attempts to
-- murder or endangers life -- is carried as a fact and not decided, on the policy
-- stated for every offence section. s 130E is different: it is a punishment SECTION,
-- and this subject now encodes those, so `the punishment for genocide` is computed
-- from the Genocide record with the Chapter 3 vocabulary.
--
-- s 130C applies "while in or out of Singapore", so it needs no place fact.

§§ `Section 130B -- Piracy by the law of nations`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 130B(1)"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes piracy by the law of nations under Penal Code 1871 section 130B
GIVEN p IS A Piracy @desc Doing any act that, by the law of nations, is piracy. The Code adopts the international-law definition; whether the act meets it is caller-asserted.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes piracy by the law of nations` IF
    p's `does an act that by the law of nations is piracy`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 130B(2)"
GIVEN p IS A Piracy
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the piracy attracts the section 130B(2) capital punishment` IF
        `constitutes piracy by the law of nations` p
    AND p's `while committing or attempting to commit piracy murders or attempts to murder another person or does an act likely to endanger the life of another person`

§§ `Section 130C -- Piratical acts`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 130C"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes a piratical act on a Singapore ship under Penal Code 1871 section 130C
GIVEN p IS A Piracy @desc Stealing a Singapore ship; stealing, throwing overboard, damaging or destroying its cargo, supplies or fittings without lawful authority; doing or attempting a mutinous act on it; or counselling or procuring any of these. In or out of Singapore.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes a piratical act` IF
        p's `steals a Singapore ship`
    OR  p's `steals or without lawful authority throws overboard damages or destroys anything that is part of the cargo supplies or fittings in a Singapore ship`
    OR  p's `does or attempts to do a mutinous act on a Singapore ship`
    OR  p's `counsels or procures a person to do any of those things`

§§ `Section 130D -- Genocide`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 130D"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes genocide under Penal Code 1871 section 130D
GIVEN g IS A Genocide @desc With intent to destroy, in whole or in part, a national, ethnical, racial or religious group: killing members; causing serious bodily or mental harm; inflicting conditions of life calculated to destroy the group; preventing births; or forcibly transferring children.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes genocide` IF
        g's `intends to destroy in whole or in part a national ethnical racial or religious group`
    AND (   g's `kills members of the group`
         OR g's `causes serious bodily or mental harm to members of the group`
         OR g's `deliberately inflicts on the group conditions of life calculated to bring about its physical destruction in whole or in part`
         OR g's `imposes measures intended to prevent births within the group`
         OR g's `forcibly transfers children of the group to another group`)

§§ `Section 130E -- Punishment for genocide`

-- Death if the offence consists of the killing of any person; otherwise imprisonment
-- for life or up to 20 years. Only the s 130D(a) limb is a killing.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 130E"
@export Give the punishment prescribed for genocide under Penal Code 1871 section 130E
GIVEN g IS A Genocide @desc The genocide facts. Death where the offence consists of killing; otherwise imprisonment for life or up to 20 years.
GIVETH A Punishment
DECIDE `the punishment for genocide` g IS
    IF g's `kills members of the group`
    THEN `death only`
    ELSE `imprisonment for life or up to` 20

§§ `Proposed Act wrappers`

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed act constitutes piracy` IF
        (   `constitutes piracy by the law of nations` (a's `piracy`)
         OR `constitutes a piratical act` (a's `piracy`))
    AND NOT (`the act is taken outside offence by Chapter 4 or Chapter 4A` a)

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed act constitutes genocide` IF
        `constitutes genocide` (a's `genocide`)
    AND NOT (`the act is taken outside offence by Chapter 4 or Chapter 4A` a)
